Subject: Re: How to plot time series of monthly values in ggplot
Message-ID: <pa2afK91p9A.B3cxKsFYBgAJ@ggplot2.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <pa2afK91p9A.4WZwMEyaBwAJ@ggplot2.groups.google.com>
References: <pa2afK91p9A.ze1KRHKjBgAJ@ggplot2.groups.google.com> <pa2afK91p9A.4WZwMEyaBwAJ@ggplot2.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/ggplot2/c/pa2afK91p9A/m/B3cxKsFYBgAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

I normally do this by putting my data through the zoo package as
zooreg(). and then using autoplot.zoo() which gives an x axis in
scale_x_yearmon() where you can specify how the dates are represented.
Zoo formats (and the related xts ones) have the advantage that there
are a lot of time series analysis methods that work for them.

Paul Bivand

